  "note": "Anonymous GET-only capture plan for the IPVanish offline clone, executed by tools/capture_source.py over a local Playwright chromium carrying an ordinary Chrome UA. The UA is a rendering-fidelity requirement, not an access-control bypass: the source serves UA-dependent markup and its Cloudflare edge returns a 403 challenge to the headless UA on support.ipvanish.com. No login, registration, form submission, payment or source mutation occurs anywhere in this plan; IPVanish has no free tier or web trial, so authenticated surfaces are unobtainable and are recorded unavailable rather than inferred. Interaction-dependent states (the three billing-period tabs, the feature expander, nav dropdowns, the mobile menu, the SSO sign-in and recovery views, the checkout payment-method chooser and its card/registration form, the support centre, and the not-found view) belong to capture_states.py, which additionally aborts every non-GET request at the network layer and refuses to fill or submit anything on the checkout origin. Localized country trees (/au, /ca, /de, /es, /fi, /fr, /gb, /ie, /it, /nl, /no, /pl, /pt, /pt-br, /se) duplicate this English tree and are declared omissions. Expect a WPML 'registered on wpml.org as a development site' banner in production markup — a source property to reproduce, not tidy away.",
